{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Red hides.</b> They were dyed red after processing." "<b>Tachash hides.</b> A species of animal, and it existed only for that hour, and it had many colors — therefore it is translated סַסְגּוֹנָא, that rejoices and prides itself in its colors (Shabbat 28)." "<b>And acacia wood.</b> And where did they have it in the wilderness? Rabbi Tanchuma explained: our father Jacob foresaw with the holy spirit that Israel was destined to build the Tabernacle in the wilderness, and he brought cedars to Egypt and planted them, and commanded his sons to take them along when they went up from Egypt."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:22.143494629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}